tests: store synchronously in testAccount and testAccountList on Cygwin

The tests call account->sync() (an asynchronous store) and delete the
manager without running an event loop. The store keeps the accounts DB
open (its -shm file stays mapped), and Cygwin cannot unlink an open file,
so clearDb() of the following tests fails with EBUSY and the old accounts
stay. testObjectsLifetime and testAccountList then fail.

---
--- a/tests/tst_libaccounts.cpp
+++ b/tests/tst_libaccounts.cpp
@@ -186,7 +186,11 @@
 
     // make sure there is account
     Account *account = mgr->createAccount(NULL);
+#ifdef __CYGWIN__
+    account->syncAndBlock();
+#else
     account->sync();
+#endif
 
     //now we get account
     account2 = mgr->account(1);
@@ -248,7 +252,11 @@
 
     // make sure there is account
     Account *account = mgr->createAccount(NULL);
+#ifdef __CYGWIN__
+    account->syncAndBlock();
+#else
     account->sync();
+#endif
 
     AccountIdList list = mgr->accountList(NULL);
     QVERIFY(!list.isEmpty());
